    <item>
      <title>1.0.0-rc.13</title>
      <pubDate>Thu, 01 Oct 2026 06:18:37 GMT</pubDate>
      <sparkle:version>202610010616</sparkle:version>
      <sparkle:shortVersionString>1.0.0-rc.13</sparkle:shortVersionString>
      <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>13.3</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
      <sparkle:channel>beta</sparkle:channel>
      <link>https://github.com/xuancongwen/bellow-app/releases/tag/v1.0.0-rc.13</link>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Bellow 1.0.0-rc.13&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Faster cleanup:&lt;/b&gt; the cleanup models now run in llama.cpp instead of Ollama, cleaning a dictation in about a third of a second on Max, with the same memory use.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;New Tiny model&lt;/b&gt; for the quickest answers in the least memory. Choose it in Settings; its edits are weaker than Standard's.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fast is gone:&lt;/b&gt; it was slower and less accurate than Standard on the new engine. If you chose it, Bellow goes back to Automatic.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Invented numbers are caught:&lt;/b&gt; if the cleanup writes a number you never said, Bellow types your words as spoken.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Requires macOS 13.3 or newer. Your downloaded models are reused, so nothing is downloaded again.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://github.com/xuancongwen/bellow-app/releases/tag/v1.0.0-rc.13"&gt;Release notes&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
</description>
      <enclosure url="https://github.com/xuancongwen/bellow-app/releases/download/v1.0.0-rc.13/Bellow-1.0.0-rc.13-macOS-arm64.dmg" length="20227876" type="application/octet-stream" sparkle:edSignature="s+YYKr6h0qTYjNdnETQgyc47Nex84sEokVaJu1lDRT7jqDXMrpa2iI+PJ9mFsX7HnNg8PnYjr1DjwH/929ZBDg==" />
